{title: Have Thine Own Way, Lord}
{artist: Adelaide A. Pollard / George C. Stebbins}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: F}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Have Thine own way, [Bb]Lord! [F]Have Thine own [C]way!
[F]Thou art the [Bb]Potter, [F]I am the [C]clay
[F]Mold me and [Bb]make me [F]after Thy [Dm]will
[Gm]While I am [F]waiting, [C]yielded and [F]still
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Have Thine own way, [Bb]Lord! [F]Have Thine own [C]way!
[F]Search me and [Bb]try me, [F]Master, to[C]day!
[F]Whiter than [Bb]snow, Lord, [F]wash me just [Dm]now
[Gm]As in Thy [F]presence [C]humbly I [F]bow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Have Thine own way, [Bb]Lord! [F]Have Thine own [C]way!
[F]Wounded and [Bb]weary, [F]help me, I [C]pray!
[F]Power, all [Bb]power, [F]surely is [Dm]Thine!
[Gm]Touch me and [F]heal me, [C]Savior di[F]vine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Have Thine own way, [Bb]Lord! [F]Have Thine own [C]way!
[F]Hold o'er my [Bb]being [F]absolute [C]sway!
[F]Fill with Thy [Bb]Spirit [F]till all shall [Dm]see
[Gm]Christ only, [F]always, [C]living in [F]me
{end_of_verse}
